description:
**Excited to grow your career?**  



BBVA is a global company with more than 160 years of history that operates in more than 25 countries where we serve more than 80 million customers. We are more than 121,000 professionals working in multidisciplinary teams with profiles as diverse as financiers, legal experts, data scientists, developers, engineers and designers.


**Learn more about the area:**  



Leveraging our knowledge across Global Operations in alignment with our three strategic axes and the Groupʼs strategic priorities.


* Knowledge \& Capacity Building . We design and deliver training plans, promote inter\-team exchanges, and develop robust succession and recognition programs to grow a winning team. We host Ops Academies to spread knowledge across the operations teams.
* Process \& Control Discipline . We model and document key operational processes, help update procedures, track incidents and audits, and maintain KPIs and dashboards that ensure transparency, resilience, and continuous improvement.
* Innovation \& Technology . We drive robotics, automation, and data initiatives, helping Transformation build scalable and future\-proofoperating models that unlock efficiency and client value.
* Governance . We assist organizing forums and maintain repositories such as Wiki Ops, contribute to initiatives, steering committees, and assist in key processes to foster cross\-geography initiatives such as the Short Term Assignments to spread best practices and innovation across BBVA.

**About the job:**

**1\. Purpose and Key Objectives:**

Provide key coordination support to the effort of the CIB Operations department in its reliable and efficient running and in achieving the sustainable growth of the CIB lines of business. This shall be done through close collaboration and alignment with all relevant stakeholders, including:


* CIB Operations teams globally;
* CIB Businesses: Global Markets, GTB, IB\&F;
* Transversal, support and control functions: Group Engineering, CIB Engineering, CIB Finance, CIB Internal Control, Internal Audit, Compliance, Accounting, etc.

**2\. Key Responsibilities:**

Key support for the facilitation of the definition and implementation of the strategic vision of CIB Operations through;


* Steering the performance,
* Governance, organisational set up and culture of CIB Operations;
* One of the representatives of CIB Operations for transversal strategic, governance, regulatory and organisational topics.

**3\. Key Tasks:**

Strategic steering and performance monitoring:


* Preparation, documentation, articulation and communication of outcomes of strategic workshops;
* Preparation and coordination of budget and resource planning and definition of operational excellence targets to CIB Operations teams;
* Monitoring and communication of the progress of key strategic initiatives;
* Monitoring of CIB operations performance.

Governance, organisational set up and culture:


* Support the definition of the organisational set up, mandates and culture underpinning the delivery of the strategic objectives;
* Definition of forums / committees and participants (including for forums not chaired by CIB Operations;
* Coordination of the implementation of new regulatory and governance processes in CIB Operations;
* Oversight for risk\-based reviews of existing governance frameworks;
* Definition and monitoring of CIB Operations' key performance indicators for governance (e.g. internal and external audit points resolution, process breaches, etc.).

**4\. Level of Complexity \& Risk Involved:**

The purpose of the Head of CIB Operations Excellence is to support the department's effort in ensuring its targets are achieved with the lowest operational, regulatory and compliance risk and highest sustainability possible. The complexity of the role is derived from the very large number of stakeholders and potentially conflicting interests that may arise due for example to finite resources or ambitious timelines. The main risk attached to the function is inaccurate, partial information leading to an inability to take decisions or taking sub\-optimal decisions. Such risk will be managed through establishing a strong focus on creating highly pertinent, transparent and cost efficient activity information databases allowing the production of impactful management information.


**5\. Requirements:**

* More than 7 years' experience working in the Corporate \& Investment Banking industry and/or in Banking Operations, Consulting, Business Processing, Target Operating Models;
* Experience in contributing to transformational initiatives;
* Ability and experience in working with professionals of multiple expertise and seniority levels;
* Strong leadership and interpersonal skills including excellent communication and presentation skills;
* High degree of proactive behavior, creativity, and accuracy;
* High dedication to the team and the bank;
* Reliable, trustworthy and high level of integrity.
* Minimum C1 level of English.

**6\. Management Responsibilities:**

* Member of the CIB Operations Management Team;
* Responsibility for a team of 3 people currently.

**Skills:**

Operational Excellence, Operational Risks, Team Management, Time Management

**We power people’s progress.**
 At Preply, we’re all about creating life\-changing learning experiences. We help people discover the magic of the perfect tutor, craft a personalised learning journey, and stay motivated to keep growing. Our approach is human\-led, tech\-enabled \- and it’s creating real impact.




 We’ve just reached unicorn status with a $150M Series D, accelerating our vision to transform education through human\-led, AI\-enhanced learning. Today, 100,000\+ tutors teach 90\+ languages to learners in 180 countries \- and we’re only getting started. As a category\-defining company, we’re shaping what the future of learning looks like at global scale.




 Every Preply lesson sparks change, fuels ambition, and drives progress that matters. Joining Preply means helping define the future of education at global scale, and building something that truly matters for millions of people, every day.




**Meet the team**
 At Preply, we're growing a talented Data Team to empower top\-notch decision\-making across our organization. Our team collaborates closely with various other chapters \- including product, business, and platform \- leveraging analysis, experimentation, causal inference, and machine learning.




 You’ll be embedded in cross\-functional teams, partnering with our MarTech Product Manager, Marketeers, Tech Leads, and the Data Strategy team. Check out our Tech Radar to see the tools and technologies we love using at Preply!




**What You’ll Be Doing**
* Collaborate with performance marketing teams in coming up with data solutions to support the optimization of marketing campaigns, budgets and results
* Use recommendation systems and clustering to uncover the most effective combinations of search terms, keywords, ad copies, and landing pages that maximize effectiveness of our paid search channel;
* Scale new channels and improve targeting and bidding strategies by using regression models to assign predictive weights to funnel events;
* Lead the rollout of LTV models and use early insights to guide marketing investments, product decisions, and uncover high\-leverage opportunities across the business \- including CRM, Customer Support, Refer\-a\-Friend, and more \- while proactively sharing learnings to inform cross\-functional strategy and prioritization.
* Design and analyze A/B tests to measure marketing effectiveness, applying advanced methods like causal inference to quantify incremental ROI
* Work closely with the Data Engineering team in the creation of scalable data pipelines while guaranteeing an optimal evolution of our ETL processes, as well on the adoption of new tools and frameworks;
* Contribute to cross\-company initiatives in alignment with our data organization’s vision
* Support proactively the application of predictive models in performance marketing channels;


**What You Need To Succeed**
* Extensive experience as a Data Scientist working with performance marketing teams in a B2C environment, delivering business insights and building data products;
* Knowledge of bidding, incrementality, and attribution.
* Skilled in developing and deploying machine learning models;
* Experience with experimentation (design and evaluation of A/B tests);
* Experience working in Marketplaces and/or digital businesses environments, in the context of performance marketing;
* Strong coding skills in SQL and Python;
* Creative mindset and proactive attitude towards the creation and evaluation of new solutions;
* Strong curiosity, problem solving and problem finding skills;
* Advanced written and verbal communication skills in English.


**Nice to have**
* Previous experience with causal inference techniques (e.g. geo\-lift testing, causal impact, synthetic control, difference in differences, etc.)
* Previous experience with Databricks, Snowflake, Looker;
* Previous experience with Apache Spark,
* Knowledge of data orchestration tools (e.g. dbt and Airflow).


**Why you’ll love it at Preply**
* An open, collaborative, dynamic and diverse culture;
* A generous monthly allowance for lessons on Preply.com, Learning \& Development budget and time off for your self\-development;
* A competitive financial package with equity, leave allowance and health insurance;
* Not in Barcelona? We offer an attractive relocation package to join us in our Preply Barcelona Hub
* Access to free mental health support platforms;
* Access to Gympass\-partnered wellness and gym centers throughout Spain to promote and support well\-being and physical health;
* The opportunity to unlock the potential of learners and tutors through language learning and teaching in 175 countries (and counting!).


**Our Principles**
* Care to change the world \- We are passionate about our work and care deeply about its impact to be life changing.
* We do it for learners \- For both Preply and tutors, learners are why we do what we do. Every day we focus on empowering tutors to deliver an exceptional learning experience.
* Keep perfecting \- To create an outstanding customer experience, we focus on simplicity, smoothness, and enjoyment, continually perfecting it as every detail matters.
* Now is the time \- In a fast\-paced world, it matters how quickly we act. Now is the time to make great things happen.
* Disciplined execution \- What makes us disciplined is the excellence in our execution. We set clear goals, focus on what matters, and utilize our resources efficiently.
* Dive deep \- We leverage business acumen and curiosity to investigate disparities between numbers and stories, unlocking meaningful insights to guide our decisions.
* Growth mindset \- We proactively seek growth opportunities and believe today's best performance becomes tomorrow's starting point. We humbly embrace feedback and learn from setbacks.
* Raise the bar \- We raise our performance standards continuously, alongside each new hire and promotion. We build diverse and high\-performing teams that can make a real difference.
* Challenge, disagree and commit \- We value open and candid communication, even when we don’t fully agree. We speak our minds, challenge when necessary, and fully commit to decisions once made.
* One Preply \- We prioritize collaboration, inclusion, and the success of our team over personal ambitions. Together, we support and celebrate each other's progress.


**Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion**
 Preply.com is committed to creating an inclusive environment where people of diverse backgrounds can thrive. We believe that the presence of different opinions and viewpoints is a key ingredient for our success as a multicultural Ed\-Tech company. That means that Preply will consider all applications for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, age or veteran status.

**(THE ENGLISH LANGUAGE VERSION FOLLOWS)**

**Akur8 est une scale\-up InsurTech en forte croissance dont la mission est de moderniser la manière dont les assureurs évaluent, tarifient et pilotent le risque.**

**Notre plateforme SaaS de nouvelle génération combine machine learning transparent, analytique prédictive et conception intelligente de produits afin de transformer des workflows assurantiels complexes en systèmes scalables et pilotés par la donnée.**


Soutenue par des équipes expertes en ingénierie, data, produit et actuariat, Akur8 permet aux assureurs de modéliser le risque jusqu’à **10× plus rapidement**, tout en garantissant transparence, explicabilité et conformité réglementaire.


À mesure que notre suite de produits s’élargit, nous construisons une plateforme **end\-to\-end** couvrant la tarification, le provisionnement et l’aide à la décision prospective en matière de risque — afin d’aider les assureurs à opérer efficacement dans un environnement complexe.

**Reconnue à l’international, Akur8 a notamment été distinguée par :**

* CB Insights – InsurTech 50 (2025\)
* CNBC – InsurTech Top 150 (2025\)
* InsurTech100 – Global Insurtech Top 100 (2025\)
* Professional Equality Index – 97/100 (2025\)

**Avec plus de 40 nationalités réparties dans 8 bureaux à travers le monde, nous accompagnons plus de 320 clients sur 4 continents, tout en cultivant une forte culture d’ingénierie et de produit.**


Nous sommes fiers d’être un employeur garantissant l’égalité des chances et de promouvoir un environnement inclusif, où la diversité des points de vue contribue à de meilleurs produits et décisions.

**Chez Akur8, nous transformons la tarification et le provisionnement en assurance non\-vie grâce à une plateforme propriétaire basée sur l’IA, qui permet aux actuaires et aux data scientists de concevoir des modèles transparents, qui peuvent être audités et performants.**

 **En tant que Responsable de l'accompagnement actuariel, vous jouerez un rôle clé pour aider nos clients à appliquer la plateforme Akur8 à des enjeux concrets de tarification et de provisionnement.** Vous serez en première ligne pour accompagner les équipes actuarielles et data science dans leur réussite sur la plateforme Akur8\. À l’intersection de la réflexion actuarielle, de la curiosité pour la donnée et d’une communication rigoureuse, vous contribuerez à résoudre des problématiques utilisateurs concrètes et à faire remonter des insights précieux aux équipes Product et Engineering.

 **Vous aurez un impact direct sur la tarification et le provisionnement en assurance non\-vie en contribuant aux activités suivantes :**

* **Accompagner nos clients sur leurs questions actuarielles** et sur l’utilisation de nos solutions de Pricing et Reserving ;
* **Collaborer avec nos équipes spécialisées en actuariat et en engineering** afin de garantir une résolution rapide et fiable des demandes ;
* **Développer des relations solides avec nos clients et partager leurs retours avec les équipes Product et Engineering** afin d’améliorer l’expérience utilisateur et l’adoption de la plateforme ;
* **Suivre l’utilisation et l’engagement des clients sur la plateforme** afin d’identifier de manière proactive les risques et les opportunités de croissance ;
* **Participer à l’onboarding des nouveaux clients** à travers des sessions de formation et un accompagnement sur les premiers projets ;
* **Contribuer aux points de suivi clients et aux ateliers d’adoption** afin de renforcer l’engagement des utilisateurs sur la plateforme ;
* **Construire des bases de connaissances internes** adaptées à des lignes métier et à des marchés spécifiques ;
* **Fournir des retours actionnables à l’équipe Product** pour orienter le développement de nouvelles fonctionnalités et les améliorations produit ;
* **Contribuer à l’optimisation des processus internes** et au renforcement de la collaboration entre les équipes ASM, ADS et Engineering ;
* **Orienter les clients vers les ressources en self\-service** (documentation, base de connaissances, FAQ) afin de favoriser une utilisation autonome ;
* **Promouvoir les bonnes pratiques en actuariat et en data science** dans le cadre des projets clients ;
* **Collaborer avec les équipes commerciales** afin d’apporter un soutien fonctionnel aux opportunités d’upsell, de cross\-sell et de renouvellement, en fonction de la santé et de l’engagement des clients.

 **Le poste est rattaché à notre bureau de Montréal, avec des déplacements occasionnels à prévoir dans le cadre d’événements professionnels.**


Vous êtes actuellement inscrit(e) dans un **programme de Master**, idéalement dans le **domaine de l’actuariat**. Les candidat(e)s issu(e)s d’autres formations techniques pourront également être considéré(e)s s’ils ou elles démontrent une bonne connaissance du secteur de l’assurance. Vous êtes à la recherche d’un stage de fin d’études (**Master 2**), à partir de Mai 2026\.

**Le ou la candidat(e) idéal(e) répond aux critères suivants :**

* Bonne **compréhension des modèles actuariels**, des données d’assurance et des techniques de modélisation prédictive (par exemple GLM, GBM) ;
* Excellentes compétences relationnelles et de communication ;
* Esprit orienté résolution de problèmes, avec une **approche proactive** face aux besoins des clients ;
* Personne organisée, structurée, capable de concilier support réactif et accompagnement proactif ;
* Une première **expérience dans des fonctions liées à la tarification en assurance** n’est pas obligatoire, mais sera considérée comme un atout ;
* Maîtrise de l’**anglais**. L’espagnol constituera un avantage significatif, et toute langue supplémentaire sera appréciée.

 *Important : Vous devez être légalement autorisé(e) à travailler à Montréal (Québec).*

**En tant que nouveau·elle venu·e, vous rejoindrez une équipe diverse, hautement qualifiée et motivée, avec un fort ADN Tech, des collègues désireux de partager leurs connaissances et leur passion.**


Mais ce n'est pas que du travail, vous ferez également partie d'une équipe dynamique qui aime passer du temps ensemble et s'amuser, notamment karaoké, déjeuners d'équipe, sports ainsi que les « happy hours » occasionnels.

**En plus de cela, nous vous fournirons :**

* Salaire compétitif
* Equipement et ordinateur moderne

**Akur8 is a fast\-growing InsurTech scale\-up on a mission to redefine insurance pricing and reserving through transparent, high\-performance modeling technology.**


Our SaaS platform uses transparent machine learning and predictive analytics to improve the speed, accuracy, and reliability of actuarial pricing and reserving.

**Built by experienced actuarial, product, and R\&D teams, Akur8’s proprietary algorithms enable insurers to generate insights up to 10x faster than traditional methods, while maintaining full explainability and regulatory confidence.**


As our platform expands, we provide next\-generation reserving capabilities, supporting an end\-to\-end approach to risk assessment and future claims anticipation.

**Recognized globally, Akur8 has been featured in:**

* CB Insights’ Insurtech 50 \- Top 50 InsurTech Companies 2025
* CNBC’s World Top 150 InsurTech Companies
* InsurTech100 Global \- 100 Most Innovative Insurtech Companies
* Professional Equality Index (2025 score of 97/100\)

 **With 40\+ nationalities across 8 global offices, we serve 320\+ insurance clients on 4 continents, partnering with insurers in mature and highly regulated markets.**

*We are proud to be an equal opportunities employer, committed to diversity, equity, and inclusion, and we evaluate all candidates fairly based on skills, experience, and professional merit.*

**At Akur8, we’re transforming non\-life insurance pricing and reserving through a proprietary AI\-driven platform that empowers actuaries and data scientists to build transparent, auditable, and efficient models.**

**As an Actuarial Success Manager, you’ll play a key role in helping clients apply Akur8’s platform to real\-world pricing and reserving challenges.** You’ll be on the front line helping actuarial and data science teams succeed on Akur8’s platform. You’ll blend actuarial thinking, data curiosity, and precise communication to solve real user problems and feed insights back into Product and Engineering.

**You will directly impact non\-life insurance pricing and reserving by driving the following activities:**

* **Assist our clients with actuarial queries** \& use of our Pricing \& Reserving solutions;
* **Collaborate with our specialist Actuarial \& Engineering teams** to ensure timely, accurate query resolution;
* **Build strong client relationships and share feedback with Product and Engineering teams** to enhance user experience and platform adoption;
* **Monitor client platform usage and engagement** to identify risks and growth opportunities proactively;
* **Assist in onboarding new clients** through training sessions and initial project support;
* **Support client check\-ins and adoption workshops** to deepen user engagement with the platform;
* **Build internal knowledge bases** tailored to specific lines of business and markets;
* **Provide actionable feedback to the Product team** to guide feature development and product improvements;
* **Help streamline internal processes** and enhance collaboration across ASM, ADS, and Engineering teams;
* **Direct clients to self\-service resources** (documentation, knowledge base, FAQs) to foster independent use;
* **Promote actuarial and data science best practices** across customer projects;
* **Partner with commercial teams** to functionally support upsell, cross\-sell, and renewal opportunities based on client health and engagement.

**You’ll be attached to our Montréal office, and occasional travel for business events will be required.**


You are currently enrolled in a **Master’s degree program**, ideally in the **actuarial domain**. Candidates with other technical academic backgrounds may be considered if they demonstrate knowledge on the insurance industry. You are looking for an end\-of\-studies internship (in Master 2\), starting from Mai 2026\.


Ideal candidates matches the following criteria:

* Solid **understanding of actuarial models**, insurance data, and predictive modeling techniques (e.g. GLM, GBMs).
* Strong interpersonal and communication skills.
* Problem\-solving mindset with a **proactive attitude** toward customer needs.
* Organized, structured, and capable of balancing reactive support and proactive engagement.
* Previous **experience in roles related to insurance pricing** are not mandatory, but they will be seen as a plus.
* Proficient in **English**. Spanish will be seen as a strong positive differentiator, additional languages are a plus.

*Important**: You must possess an employment status that allows you to work in Montréal (Québec).*

**As a newcomer, you'll be joining a diverse, highly skilled and motivated team, with a strong Tech DNA, colleagues that are eager to share their knowledge and passion.**


We care about strong teamwork and a positive day\-to\-day environment. The team regularly connects through optional activities such as team lunches, sports, karaoke, or occasional after\-work gatherings.


In addition to this, we will provide you with:

* Competitive internship compensation
* Top\-notch laptop and equipement

**Corporate Profile**



SyBridge Technologies is at the forefront of technology\-enabled design, prototyping, and manufacturing solutions for complex, high\-precision parts. Our mission is to revolutionize how parts are designed and manufactured, making the process simpler and faster through advanced technology. As North America's largest injection molding tooling platform and the leading private on\-demand digital manufacturer, we're driven by our cutting\-edge AI/ML technology and a team of top\-tier software engineers, computational geometry experts, and data scientists. Backed by Crestview Partners and built on 15 strategic acquisitions, SyBridge is a powerhouse of innovation and growth. Headquartered in Itasca, Illinois, we operate across 18 locations in North America, Europe, and Asia. Discover more at www.SyBridge.com.

 **About Crestview Partners**



Founded in 2004, Crestview is a value\-oriented private equity firm focused on the middle market. The firm is based in New York and manages funds with approximately $10 billion of aggregate capital commitments. The firm is led by a group of partners who have complementary experience and backgrounds in private equity, finance, operations, and management. Crestview has senior investment professionals focused on sourcing and managing investments in industrials, media, and financial services. For more information, please visit www.crestview.com.

 **Position Summary**



In support of the Mission and Vision of SyBridge Technologies Inc., the **CNC Machinist** is responsible for programming and operating a CNC machine to build tools using 3D models. Reporting to the Machining Leader, the **CNC Machinist** ensures first time quality is a priority each and every time while also achieving time allowances for each job assigned.

 **Key Responsibilities**



On a daily basis:


* Import, manipulate, and process 3D models;
* Machine steel with close attention to health and safety requirements;
* Use tools and machinery provided; program, setup and operate the CNC machine using 3\-AXIS, and powermill 5Aixs.
* Machine mold plates, components, cores and cavities; holding tolerances as tight as less than 0\.0005;
* Verify dimensions of machined parts using precision measuring instruments/probe to ensure first time quality;
* Complete checklists and report deviations from specified tolerances;
* Maintain continuity among work shifts by documenting and communicating actions, irregularities, and continuing needs using provided paper and/or electronic logs;
* Utilize FCS toe clamping and chucks for setup and fixturing.





As required:


* Assist in the repair of machine tools and parts, as needed;
* Maintain safe operations by keeping work area clean and organized and by adhering to safety procedures and regulations;
* Maintain the equipment by completing basic preventive maintenance requirements; following manufacturer's instructions, initiating repair work orders, etc.;
* Participate in required meetings and training, as requested.




**Qualifications**


* High school diploma or equivalent is required.
* Three (3\) years of related experience operating CNC;
* Three (3\) years’ experience programming CNC machines (3\-AXIS, Powermill software is an asset);
* Ability to operate multiple machines at a time and work in a team environment;
* Powermill experience
* Ability to perform under pressure and work independently;
* Ability to prioritize tasks and meet deadlines as required;
* Ability to ensure quality standards are met;
* Strong attention to detail and analytical skills
* Proficient in time management and communication skills




**What We Offer**


* Competitive compensation
* Comprehensive benefits
* Performance\-based rewards and recognition
* Supportive and inclusive work environment
* Career growth and development opportunities





Join us at SyBridge Technologies and be a part of a team that's shaping the future of manufacturing!



Our Commitment to You



SyBridge Technologies is an Equal Opportunity Employer and prohibits Discrimination and Harassment of any kind. We are committed to the attitude of equal employment opportunity for all employees and to providing employees with a work environment free of discrimination and harassment. All employment decisions at SyBridge are based on business needs, job requirements, and individual qualifications, without regard to race, color, religion or belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran or disability status, family or parental status, or any other status protected by the laws or regulations in the locations where we operate. SyBridge encourages applicants of all ages.



In accordance with the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA), 2005 and the Ontario Human Rights Code, and the Equal Employment Opportunity Employment Commission, SyBridge Technologies Inc. will provide accommodations throughout the recruitment selection and/or assessment process to applicants with disabilities. If selected to participate in the recruitment, selection and/or assessment process, please inform SyBridge Technologies Inc. Human Resources staff of the nature of the accommodation(s) that you may require to ensure your accommodation and inclusion.
